  "boundary": "Box/Laschen, Janus and Two-Cut own SET/STEP/CAPTURE/RETURN, state and checkpoint storage. The Box scope includes fold controls, one selected integer/totient profile, the explicit 1111 layer witness P0/F10, P1/F26 or P2/F42, and the source-owned CON-DAO next cursor/display/stopped-timer checkpoint. Other number profiles keep the layer field at HOLD. Native commands stop playback before capture; no running wall-clock phase is claimed exact. Host validates scoped Return and collects typed, last-observed states, not a simultaneous whole-machine state. One explicit embedded source at a time; unload discards its context. Existing PENT/LIFE03/phase exports remain separate typed records. No automatic shared clock or cross-carrier identity.",
